  "id": "mutism",
  "term": "mutism",
  "definition": "Mutism is a condition in which a person cannot produce spoken words even though they can understand speech. It can occur with mental disorders or brain disease, and may also appear as selective mutism, in which a child consistently does not speak in social situations despite speaking to certain people.",
